BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Farm Table at Spruce Peak: Runamok Maple & Vermont Wagyu
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTSTAMP:20261007T175136Z
UID:19831ba1ce1accce8dd72fbe87cb0c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:This October evening embraces the depth and abundance of late
 ‑season Vermont\, highlighting producers known for their patience\, prec
 ision\, and respect for craft. Runamok’s thoughtfully produced maple syr
 ups will be woven throughout the menu with restraint and balance\, while V
 ermont Wagyu provides an elegant\, richly flavored foundation for the meal
 . Hosted indoors around the hearth\, the setting reflects the transition i
 nto fall—warm\, intimate\, and grounded in tradition. The menu leans int
 o heartier preparations\, longer cooking\, and layered flavors\, taking cu
 es from the season as the growing year comes to a close.\n\nSources: Vermo
 nt.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:The Lodge at Spruce Peak\, 7412 Mountain Rd
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/farm-table
 -at-spruce-peak-runamok-maple-vermont-wagyu-25-09-2026-17-29-58
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Oct 7 | Mary Oliver: Saved By the Beauty of the World film screeni
 ng
DTSTART:20261007T190000
DTEND:20261007T210000
DTSTAMP:20261007T175136Z
UID:e71a1c8d54881d4b520520f18d8443@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:This event is sold out. Please click here to join the wait lis
 t . "I got saved by poetry\, and I got saved by the beauty of the world." 
 — Mary Oliver Join Vermont Public and Adventure Dinner for a screening o
 f Mary Oliver: Saved by the Beauty of the World . The film from PBS’ Ame
 rican Masters reveals the life and career of the best-selling poet and the
  inspiration behind her renowned works. Mary Oliver was known for her insi
 ghtful writing on nature\, beauty\, and love. Enjoy a cozy fall evening at
  the Clubhouse\; mix and mingle with other poetry fans\; peruse a selectio
 n of poetry books for sale from Phoenix Books \; enjoy free popcorn and a 
 cash bar with beer\, wine and non-alcoholic beverages. Plus\, a special re
 ading from Vermont poet laureate Bianca Stone . Watch a preview of the fil
 m featuring archival clips and interviews with Stephen Colbert\, Oprah Win
 frey\, Steve Buscemi\, Lucy Dacus and more: https://www.youtube.com/watch?
 v=B7bfYkgotBM Click here to reserve your ticket. Schedule 6 p.m. - doors o
 pen | cash bar available 7 p.m. - welcome reading from Bianca Stone + scre
 ening 8:30 p.m. - mingling 9 p.m. - event ends Tickets General Admission -
  $5 Generous Admission - $10 PLEASE NOTE : The event is on the second floo
 r and does not have elevator access. Accommodations Vermont Public is comm
 itted to providing access and accommodation for individuals with disabilit
 ies at our events. To request accommodations\, please email events@vermont
 public.org or call us at 802-655-9451 at least seven days in advance of th
 e event. Cancellation Policy Please let us know by emailing events@vermont
 public.org if you are not able to join us so that we may release your tick
 ets to someone else. If tickets are able to be resold\, we are happy to of
 fer a refund\, minus the processing fees. Directions and Parking The Adven
 ture Dinner Clubhouse is located at 70 Roosevelt Hwy\, Colchester\, VT 054
 46 . Plenty of free parking is located near the venue. Photo Credit Mary s
 eated on sofa with dogs\, early 1990s. © NW Orchard\, LLC courtesy of the
  Library of Congress Other questions? Email us at events@vermontpublic.org
  . Adventure Dinner Clubhouse\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/oct-7-mary
 -oliver-saved-by-the-beauty-of-the-world-film-screening-02-09-2026-11-29-4
 4
END:VEVENT
